# Cloudflare Pages cache policy (apps/web/public/_headers -> served at the site root).
# Content-hashed build assets are immutable and cached forever; everything else (HTML documents,
# the service worker, the manifest) must revalidate so a new deploy is visible on the NEXT normal
# load — no hard refresh needed.

/_next/static/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/sw.js
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

/manifest.webmanifest
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Security headers for every document — all 19 player-facing brand domains AND the operator
# console (triocodes.com). The API tier already sets its own set (apps/api/src/http.ts
# applySecurityHeaders); the web tier had none at all, which is the gap this closes.
#
# Why the web tier needs this MORE than a typical site: the session bearer token is kept in
# localStorage (src/lib/auth/session.ts) with no HttpOnly cookie backstop, so any script that
# executes in this origin — a stored XSS in a community post, a chat message, a username, an
# admin-set brand field, or one compromised npm dependency — walks off with a durable token, up
# to platform_superadmin on the console host.
#
# `_headers` is a Cloudflare Pages deploy artifact: `next dev` never reads it, so nothing below
# affects the local dev loop and no localhost origin needs allowing. It is also the ONLY place
# these can be set — the app runs on the Edge runtime via next-on-pages, where a Next.js
# `headers()` entry is not honoured for the static/edge output Pages serves.
#
# Per-header reasoning (the rule block itself must stay one header per line):
#
# Content-Security-Policy
#   default-src 'self'      — nothing loads from anywhere unless a directive below says so.
#   script-src              — 'unsafe-inline' is UNAVOIDABLE here and that is a real limitation,
#                             not an oversight. Next 14's App Router streams the RSC payload as
#                             inline `<script>self.__next_f.push(...)</script>` tags whose content
#                             differs per request and per route, so no hash list can cover them,
#                             and there is a second inline script in app/layout.tsx (the
#                             pre-paint theme init). A nonce is the correct fix but CANNOT come
#                             from a static file — it has to be minted per response, which means
#                             src/middleware.ts setting the CSP and Next picking the nonce up.
#                             That is the follow-up; it is owned by another file.
#                             'strict-dynamic' is not an option either: it needs a nonce or hash
#                             to bootstrap from, so with neither it would block EVERY script and
#                             take the whole app down.
#                             What 'self' still buys with 'unsafe-inline' present: no EXTERNAL
#                             script file can load. The usual stored-XSS payload is a short
#                             injection that pulls a stage-2 from an attacker host, and that is
#                             blocked — as is a compromised CDN. What it does NOT buy: inline
#                             script injected into our own HTML still runs, can read the token,
#                             and can still exfiltrate by navigation or by an <img> URL. This is
#                             defence in depth, not an XSS fix; the fix is an HttpOnly cookie.
#                             'unsafe-eval' is deliberately absent — nothing here needs eval
#                             (verified against the built client chunks).
#   style-src 'unsafe-inline' — genuinely required, not assumed: ~39 components pass React
#                             `style={{…}}` and layout.tsx sets the whole per-brand palette as an
#                             inline style attribute on <html> via brandRootStyle(), which CSP
#                             covers under style-src-attr. Without it every brand loses its
#                             colours. fonts.googleapis.com is the per-brand Google Fonts
#                             stylesheet (lib/brand/fonts.ts).
#   font-src                — fonts.gstatic.com serves the actual face files for that stylesheet.
#   img-src https:          — deliberately open to any https host, because a brand's logo_url and
#                             favicon_url are operator-set arbitrary URLs in the DB (console →
#                             brand settings). Pinning this would silently break the logo on any
#                             brand pointing at its own CDN, which is the kind of breakage that
#                             gets a CSP reverted wholesale. It does leave an exfiltration channel
#                             open; that is the price of not breaking 19 live brands.
#   media-src               — chat voice notes and video attachments are served by the API
#                             (lib/chat/liveChat.ts mediaUrl); blob: covers locally recorded audio.
#   connect-src             — the REST API and the wss:// game engine. These are inlined at BUILD
#                             time from NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL / NEXT_PUBLIC_WS_URL and are the
#                             SAME for production and preview (HOSTING.md §3.2), so hardcoding
#                             them here is safe. ⚠ IF EITHER OF THOSE ENV VARS EVER CHANGES HOST,
#                             THIS LINE MUST CHANGE IN THE SAME COMMIT or every brand goes dead
#                             (no login, no ticks). This directive is the main win of the whole
#                             policy: a stolen localStorage token cannot be fetch()ed, XHR'd,
#                             sendBeacon'd or WebSocket'd to an attacker origin.
#   frame-src https:        — the PayHero Lipwa checkout is embedded in an iframe
#                             (components/wallet/LipwaDeposit.tsx) from a per-brand
#                             operator-configured `lipwa_url` (gatewayschema.ts), so the host is
#                             not knowable here. Pinning app.payhero.africa would break card
#                             deposits for any brand on a different checkout host. Note this does
#                             NOT weaken the clickjacking defence — that is frame-ancestors.
#   worker-src/manifest-src — /sw.js and /manifest.webmanifest, both same-origin.
#   base-uri 'self'         — blocks an injected <base href> from silently repointing every
#                             relative script and form URL in the document at an attacker host.
#   form-action 'self'      — no form in this app posts off-origin, so a planted login form
#                             cannot POST a password or a withdrawal to a third party.
#   object-src 'none'       — no Flash/applet/plugin surface at all.
#   frame-ancestors 'none'  — see X-Frame-Options below.
#
# Strict-Transport-Security
#   Two years, matching the API's max-age, with includeSubDomains. `preload` is deliberately NOT
#   asserted. These are 19 apex domains belonging to CLIENTS, not to us: the preload token is a
#   claim that the apex and every subdomain under it will be HTTPS-only forever, it lets anyone
#   submit the domain to the browser-baked preload list, and removal then takes months and a
#   browser release — with no user override if a client still runs an http-only mail or cPanel
#   subdomain. That is not a commitment a shared static header file should make on someone else's
#   behalf. The API, a single domain we own, keeps its preload. includeSubDomains is kept because
#   every brand zone is fronted by Cloudflare with SSL already, but it carries the same
#   subdomain-forcing caveat and is worth re-checking before onboarding a brand with legacy
#   plain-HTTP subdomains.
#
# X-Frame-Options: DENY (+ the CSP frame-ancestors above, for browsers that prefer it)
#   The deposit amount field and the withdrawal confirm button are one-click, irreversible,
#   real-money controls. Framed and overlaid, they are a textbook clickjack.
#
# X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
#   A user-uploaded KYC document or chat attachment proxied through this origin must never be
#   re-sniffed into text/html and executed as a page in the session's own origin.
#
# Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
#   This one is load-bearing, not boilerplate. Real capability tokens travel in QUERY STRINGS —
#   `?t=<hmac>` on /kyc/file/:id and /chat/media/:id, `?token=` on /w/act — and this origin loads
#   a third-party stylesheet (Google Fonts, per brand). With no policy, the full URL of the page
#   goes out as the Referer, which hands a national-ID document link or a withdrawal-approval
#   link to every third-party origin the page touches. The API uses the stricter `no-referrer`;
#   the web tier cannot, because same-origin navigations here legitimately read the referrer, so
#   this sends the full URL only same-origin and bare origin cross-origin.
#
# Permissions-Policy
#   Deny every device/sensor feature this app does not use. `microphone=(self)` stays because chat
#   voice notes call getUserMedia (components/chat/ChatParts.tsx); `autoplay`/`fullscreen` stay at
#   self for the trade sounds and the chart. `payment` and `clipboard-write` are deliberately NOT
#   listed: the PayHero checkout iframe carries allow="payment; clipboard-write", and denying
#   either here would revoke that delegation and break card deposits. Their browser defaults are
#   already `self`, so leaving them out loses nothing.
#
# X-Permitted-Cross-Domain-Policies: none
#   Matches the API — no Adobe cross-domain policy file is honoured for this origin.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com; font-src 'self' data: https://fonts.gstatic.com; img-src 'self' data: blob: https:; media-src 'self' blob: https://invest254-api.fly.dev; connect-src 'self' https://invest254-api.fly.dev wss://invest254-engine-pm.fly.dev; frame-src https:; worker-src 'self'; manifest-src 'self'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; object-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: accelerometer=(), ambient-light-sensor=(), autoplay=(self), bluetooth=(), browsing-topics=(), camera=(), display-capture=(), encrypted-media=(), fullscreen=(self), geolocation=(), gyroscope=(), hid=(), idle-detection=(), local-fonts=(), magnetometer=(), midi=(), microphone=(self), screen-wake-lock=(), serial=(), usb=(), window-management=(), xr-spatial-tracking=()
  X-Permitted-Cross-Domain-Policies: none
